    {
      "id": "generic-fast-tanh-float",
      "name": "generic_fast_tanh_float",
      "category": "MathFunctionsImpl",
      "signature": "generic_fast_tanh_float(A X)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "A X",
          "type": "T&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<T> T",
      "docs": "\\internal \\returns the hyperbolic tan of \\a a (coeff-wise)\nDoesn't do anything fancy, just a 13/6-degree rational interpolant which\nis accurate up to a couple of ulps in the (approximate) range [-8, 8],\noutside of which tanh(x) = +/-1 in single precision. The input is clamped\nto the range [-c, c]. The value c is chosen as the smallest value where\nthe approximation evaluates to exactly 1. In the reange [-0.0004, 0.0004]\nthe approxmation tanh(x) ~= x is used for better accuracy as x tends to zero.\nThis implementation works on both scalars and packets."
    },
